<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Shipped in the Android binding package and imported automatically by any project
  that references it (directly or through Plugin.Maui.Intercom).

  Problem this solves:

  Intercom's Android SDK pulls in Jetpack Compose, and Xamarin.AndroidX.Compose.Runtime.Annotation
  publishes two variants that both define androidx.compose.runtime.Immutable / Stable:

      Xamarin.AndroidX.Compose.Runtime.Annotation.Android  -> aar/runtime-annotation-android.aar
      Xamarin.AndroidX.Compose.Runtime.Annotation.Jvm      -> jar/runtime-annotation-jvm.jar

  The .Jvm package adds its jar to @(AndroidJavaLibrary) whenever AndroidApplication is
  true, so an app that ends up with both on the graph fails to dex:

      Type androidx.compose.runtime.Immutable is defined multiple times

  Why it has to be fixed here and not by NuGet metadata:

  The remedy is an ExcludeAssets/PrivateAssets suppression, and a suppression describes one
  reference edge — it does not travel through NuGet dependency metadata the way a dependency
  id does. NuGet also unions assets across every path a package arrives by, so suppressing it
  on this package's edge does nothing about the edge from Compose.Runtime to the .Jvm variant
  in the consuming app. Without this file every consumer has to hand-add:

      <PackageReference Include="Xamarin.AndroidX.Compose.Runtime.Annotation.Jvm"
                        Version="..." ExcludeAssets="all" PrivateAssets="all" />

  Restore-time metadata cannot express that, but a build-time item removal can. Android wants
  the .Android variant, so the .Jvm jar is the one that goes.

  Set PluginMauiIntercomFixComposeAnnotationDuplicate=false to opt out (for example if you
  would rather manage the suppression yourself).
-->
<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PluginMauiIntercomFixComposeAnnotationDuplicate Condition=" '$(PluginMauiIntercomFixComposeAnnotationDuplicate)' == '' ">true</PluginMauiIntercomFixComposeAnnotationDuplicate>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Hook placement matters. The dexer does NOT read @(AndroidJavaLibrary) directly:
    _DetermineJavaLibrariesToCompile (Xamarin.Android.Javac.targets) feeds it to the
    DetermineJavaLibrariesToCompile task, which produces @(_JavaLibrariesToCompile) ->
    @(_JavaLibrariesToCompileForApp), and that is what D8/R8 receive. So the removal has to
    happen before that target, not before _CompileDex — _CompileDex only gathers the
    finished .dex files, and its DependsOnTargets have already dexed by the time anything
    hooked BeforeTargets="_CompileDex" runs.

    _CheckDuplicateJavaLibraries and the two apk targets also read @(AndroidJavaLibrary),
    so they are covered too.

    This runs inside a target rather than as an evaluation-time ItemGroup because the .Jvm
    package adds its jar from its own imported targets and buildTransitive import order
    between two packages is not guaranteed.
  -->
  <Target Name="_PluginMauiIntercomRemoveDuplicateComposeRuntimeAnnotation"
          Condition=" '$(PluginMauiIntercomFixComposeAnnotationDuplicate)' == 'true' AND '$(AndroidApplication)' == 'true' "
          BeforeTargets="_DetermineJavaLibrariesToCompile;_CheckDuplicateJavaLibraries;_BuildApkEmbed;_BuildApkFastDev">
    <ItemGroup>
      <AndroidJavaLibrary Remove="@(AndroidJavaLibrary->WithMetadataValue('Filename','runtime-annotation-jvm'))" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
